# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without this every text
# file lands in the working copy with CRLF. Biome formats with LF
# (biome.json sets no lineEnding override), which fails `biome check` on
# effectively every file, and
# desktop/src/features/messages/ui/virtuaWheelModePatch.test.mjs asserts on
# patches/*.patch with `\n`-joined patterns. Normalize to LF in the working
# copy on every platform; the stored blobs are already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# desktop/native-inventory.json is generated by `pnpm generate:native-inventory`
# and rewritten by any change under desktop/src-tauri, so two concurrent desktop
# PRs conflict in it every time. The conflict is never interesting: the file is
# derived, so the correct resolution is always "regenerate", never a hand-merge.
#
# merge=ours keeps the current branch's copy instead of producing conflict
# markers. That copy is then stale, which `pnpm check:native-inventory` reports
# as a clear, actionable failure ("native inventory is stale ... run
# `pnpm generate:native-inventory`") rather than a merge you have to unpick.
#
# The driver is registered by `just hooks` (and so by `just setup`). Without it
# git falls back to a normal conflict, which is the old behaviour, not a break.
desktop/native-inventory.json merge=ours
